              "feedback": {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Incorrect. Since the slow step limits the rate of reaction, first write the (elementary) rate law for that step. Then since an intermediate cannot be in the (overall) rate law, use the (elementary) rate laws for the fast, reversible step (recall that for this type of step the rate of 'forward' reaction equals the rate of 'reverse' reaction) to solve for the concentration of the intermediate. Finally, substitute this into the rate-determining step rate law to determine the (overall) rate law."
                      }
